{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"tied"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Tied-swift.struct","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLMetronomeV4NoteV4TiedV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Tied"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"<metronome-tied>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note\/tied-swift.property"]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLMetronomeV4NoteV4tiedAE4TiedVSgvp","title":"tied","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"tied"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLMetronomeV4NoteV4TiedV","text":"Tied"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/tied-swift.property"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"The metronome-tied element indicating the presence of a tie to another metronome note, if any.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Note/tied-swift.property":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"tied"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLMetronomeV4NoteV4TiedV","text":"Tied"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The metronome-tied element indicating the presence of a tie to another metronome note, if any.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note\/tied-swift.property","title":"tied","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/tied-swift.property"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLMetronome","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLMetronome","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"displayed in the music notation."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Note/Tied-swift.struct":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Tied-swift.struct","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Tied","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Tied","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome-tied indicates the presence of a tie within a metric relationship mark. As with the tied"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element, both the start and stop of the tie should be specified, in this case within separate metronome-note"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note\/tied-swift.struct","title":"MXLMetronome.Note.Tied"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Note":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Note","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Note","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome-note type defines the appearance of a note within a metric relationship mark."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note","title":"MXLMetronome.Note"}}}